// A4 — `.chars()` on an OWNED rvalue receiver (`s.trim()`). The Chars iterator borrows the receiver's bytes
// for the whole loop; the owned rvalue is materialized ONCE into a loop-scoped temp (read-once, stable) and
// dropped after the loop. ASan/LeakSanitizer-clean == the materialized `s.trim()` buffer is freed exactly once.
fn uint8 main() {
    string s = "  abc  ";
    int32 n = 0;
    foreach (char c in s.trim().chars()) { n = n + 1; }
    return cast<uint8>(n);   // "abc" -> 3 codepoints
}
